# Skill routing (mandatory)

At the **start of every new user request** (and when the request **changes direction**):

1. **Classify** the request (feature, UI, code, architecture, Archsphere data, git, question-only, etc.).
2. **Read** [skill-routing/SKILL.md](../skills/skill-routing/SKILL.md) — routing matrix, handoffs, anti-patterns.
3. **Read** each selected skill's `SKILL.md` before acting on that concern.
4. **Follow handoff order** when multiple skills apply (e.g. PM → UX → dev — not dev-first on greenfield UI).

## Token-aware defaults

| Situation | Minimum skills |
|-----------|----------------|
| Question-only (no code/data change) | None — unless the answer requires a skill workflow |
| Trivial fix (typo, one-liner) | software-development (+ qa-testing if prod code changed) |
| Code change / refactor / feature | See full matrix in skill-routing SKILL.md |

Do not skip evaluation on substantial work. Do not load the full delivery chain for trivial fixes.
